<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#denarius">Glossary</a> · Term · currency</p><h1 class="enc-title">Denarius</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The denarius was the standard <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> coin of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> for several centuries. Its progressive debasement in the third century was a sign of fiscal crisis. The name was later revived for the silver penny of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a>, established by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>'s monetary reforms as the basis of medieval European coinage.</p></div>
